.TH PKGS 1 "October 2026" "pkgs 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pkgs \- fuzzy package management for Termux and Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkgs
[COMMAND] [OPTIONS] [NAMES...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Bare invocation displays help. Install and uninstall open an fzf multi-select
picker when package names are omitted. Exact names bypass the picker.
Transactions show the manager, scope, and command and request confirmation.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install [NAMES...]
Install exact names or open the package picker.
.TP
.B uninstall [NAMES...]
Remove installed packages only. Alias: remove.
.TP
.B search [QUERY]
Read-only picker; Enter shows information.
.TP
.B list [\-\-installed] [\-\-json]
Show package inventory as readable text or JSON.
.TP
.B info NAMES...
Colorized package information, wrapped to fit the terminal preview.
.TP
.B upgrade [NAMES...]
Use the selected backend upgrade workflow. pip requires explicit names.
.TP
.B refresh
Refresh repository metadata for APT, DNF and XBPS. Use upgrade with pacman.
.TP
.B managers, doctor
Show detected managers or diagnose the environment.
.TP
.B completion SHELL [install|update|status|uninstall]
Print or manage completions for bash, zsh, or fish. --install aliases install.
.TP
.B cache clear
Remove pkgs catalog caches; does not touch package-manager caches.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-H, \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Show version.
.TP
.B \-\-manager NAME
Use apt, pacman, paru, yay, dnf, xbps, npm, uv-tool, pip, gem, or auto.
.TP
.B \-\-query TEXT
Search/filter the picker. Do not combine with exact names.
.TP
.B \-\-global
Select npm global scope. Default npm scope is the current project.
.TP
.B \-\-color MODE
Choose auto, always, or never. Auto respects NO_COLOR.
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-preview LAYOUT
fzf preview-window layout. Default: bottom:55%:wrap.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Display transaction without changing packages.
.TP
.B \-y, \-\-yes
Skip pkgs confirmation and use backend noninteractive options where supported.
.TP
.B \-\-directory DIR
Completion destination directory. Bash and Zsh installation is file-only.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Print read-only preparation phase timings to stderr.
.SH COMPLETION
Install/update writes _pkgs for Zsh or pkgs for Bash without adding startup
blocks, fpath changes, source statements, compinit, or compdef calls.
Fish retains its completion file and managed conf.d setup.
.br
Zsh uses an explicit directory, a recorded destination, or caller-supplied
FPATH. From Zsh: FPATH="$FPATH" pkgs completion zsh install.
The child process cannot inspect the parent shell's live fpath or completion state.
.br
Bash requires a recognized bash-completion loader for automatic resolution.
It respects BASH_COMPLETION_USER_DIR, otherwise XDG_DATA_HOME's user completion
directory. Installing the file does not load bash-completion in the current shell.
An explicit directory permits file-only installation with activation unverified.
.br
The application installer accepts repeatable --completion-dir SHELL=DIR.
Unknown destinations fail preflight without changing startup files. Status
reports the file, content/version, resolution, loader and activation separately.
Reload instructions are printed, never written into startup files.
.br
Exact legacy pkgs blocks are removed after backing up the startup target;
symlinks and unrelated content are preserved. Edited/malformed blocks and
foreign or edited completions are left untouched and reported.
.SH PICKER
Tab/Shift-Tab select packages. Enter accepts. Ctrl-X toggles the preview.
Alt-I hides/shows installed packages. Alt-O opens the highlighted homepage.
Esc/Ctrl-C cancel. [i] marks installed packages; [e] marks an unowned related
executable (same-name matches are candidates, not proof). Rows and list use
cached external evidence. A blank marker does not prove no external command
exists. Highlighting a package fetches current evidence in the preview without
blocking initial picker startup. Source-built ~/.fzf/bin/fzf remains supported.
.br
Read-only preparation queries have a 45-second budget; preview enrichment has
five seconds and individual ownership queries at most three seconds. Slow work
prints delayed stderr progress. Esc/Ctrl-C cancels queries and preview children.
Interactive package transactions retain native prompts and have no such timeout.
.SH FILES
~/.config/pkgs/config.json (XDG_CONFIG_HOME respected).
.br
~/.cache/pkgs/ (XDG_CACHE_HOME respected).
.br
~/.local/state/pkgs/completions.json (XDG_STATE_HOME respected); records managed
completion destinations for subsequent update/uninstall.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
FZF_DEFAULT_OPTS and FZF_DEFAULT_OPTS_FILE retain compatible fzf preferences.
NO_COLOR disables automatic ANSI colors. PKGS_FUZZY_TAB=0 requests native
completion without the bundled fuzzy Tab integration. Native candidate generation
uses local data with a 1.5-second query budget. PKGS_DEBUG=1 enables helper
stderr diagnostics. FPATH may be supplied by the invoking Zsh for one command.
Picker helpers use a controlled noninteractive Bash child without startup hooks.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Registry catalogs are not exhaustive. pip/uv queries use exact PyPI names.
Completion never searches remote registries. Native Windows is not supported.
.SH SEE ALSO
fzf(1), apt(8), pacman(8), dnf(8), xbps-query(1)
